 The spot price of RELIANCE at 1450 is 50 points below the 1500 strike, so the call is out‑of‑the‑money and will likely generate a modest premium while still leaving room for upside if the stock rallies above 1500 before expiration. Selling the covered call caps your gain at the strike plus the premium received, but you retain the downside protection of owning the shares and keep the premium if the price stays below 1500. Given the current level, selling the call is reasonable if you are comfortable limiting upside to around 1500 + premium and want to earn income; otherwise, hold the shares without the call.
